{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:45:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been feeling really nauseous, especially when I eat or drink. I threw up once last night. And I have this sharp pain in my upper belly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:46:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s been getting worse over the last two days. I’ve been trying lorazepam like I usually do, but it’s not helping this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:48:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any fever, blood in your vomit, or diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No blood, no diarrhea. I’ve had chills, but my temperature hasn’t gone above 97."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:50:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. I also see from your clinic visit earlier that there was a mix-up with your medications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:51:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I was taking three fluconazole pills and only one prednisone. I thought the pills looked different. I didn’t realize I had it backwards."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:52:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. You’re supposed to take more prednisone and just one fluconazole. That mistake may have made your graft-versus-host disease harder to control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:53:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no. Is that why I’m feeling so sick?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:54:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be part of it. We’ve restarted your prednisone at the right dose—60 mg daily. But the high dose of steroids can also irritate your stomach, which might explain the nausea and pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s the medicine helping me but also making me feel worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:57:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re going to treat the stomach irritation while keeping your immune system under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:58:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll increase your pantoprazole to twice a day and start a new medication called sucralfate. It coats the stomach to help heal the irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2151-06-13 17:59:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. Will I need any tests?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2151-06-13 18:00:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll do a CT scan of your abdomen to make sure there’s nothing else going on, like an infection or blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2151-06-13 18:01:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, I’m glad we’re checking everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2151-06-13 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your CT scan came back. Good news—it shows no signs of infection, blockage, or other problems in your abdomen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2151-06-13 20:31:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. So it’s really just the stomach irritation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2151-06-13 20:32:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. The scan was completely normal. Your symptoms are most likely due to gastritis from the increased steroid dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2151-06-13 20:33:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the chills? Are those related too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2151-06-13 20:34:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They could be. Sometimes nausea and discomfort can make you feel chilled, even without a fever. We’re not seeing signs of infection in your labs either."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2151-06-13 20:35:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2151-06-14 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I just reviewed your labs from this morning. Your liver enzymes are a bit high, but they’re at your usual baseline. We think that’s related to your GVHD, not a new problem."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2151-06-14 07:16:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So nothing new to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2151-06-14 07:17:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at all. Your tacrolimus level is good, and your blood counts are stable. You’re responding well to the treatment for your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2151-06-14 07:18:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do feel a little better. The nausea isn’t as bad this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2151-06-14 07:19:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’ll keep you on the sucralfate and higher-dose pantoprazole to let your stomach heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2151-06-14 07:20:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my prednisone? Will I stay on 60 mg?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2151-06-14 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep it at 60 mg for now to control your GVHD, but we’ll watch for side effects. We’ll also make sure you and your husband understand all your medications before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2151-06-14 07:23:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. I don’t want to make that mistake again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2151-06-14 07:24:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll go over them together. We also adjusted your oxycodone—now it’s 20 mg twice a day for your hip pain, which should be enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2151-06-14 07:25:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s fine. My hip pain is chronic, and that dose usually works."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2151-06-14 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. I just got the final report from your CT scan. It confirms no acute issues in your abdomen. The spleen and lymph nodes show old changes, likely from past infections, but nothing active."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2151-06-14 10:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like TB? Because I had the BCG vaccine years ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2151-06-14 10:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The calcifications are consistent with that. No treatment needed—it’s just a reminder of your history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you today. Your symptoms have improved, and everything looks stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:31:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What changes should I expect with my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:32:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll start sucralfate four times a day, take pantoprazole twice daily, and stay on prednisone at 60 mg for now. We’ll taper it later. Oxycodone is now 20 mg twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:33:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:34:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see your oncologist soon. They’ll help manage your prednisone taper and GVHD. Call if nausea returns or you have new symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:35:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re glad we could help. Take care, and follow those instructions closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:38:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:39:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—your liver tests are still a bit high, but we believe it’s due to GVHD, not a new issue. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:40:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I understand. I’ll keep up with my appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:41:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re doing well. We’ll get your discharge papers ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:42:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll have a nurse go over your medications one more time with you and your husband before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:45:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. I want to make sure I get it right this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:46:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. Safety first. We’re here to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:47:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:48:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll see you in follow-up, but call sooner if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:49:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, and get some rest at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2151-06-14 16:52:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2151-06-13 17:44:00",
    "admission_end": "2151-06-14 18:25:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for nausea, vomiting, and epigastric abdominal pain following a medication error in which she mistakenly took fluconazole instead of prednisone. This led to under-treatment of her chronic graft-versus-host disease, requiring re-initiation of high-dose prednisone. The increase in steroids likely worsened steroid-induced gastritis, causing her symptoms. A CT scan of the abdomen and pelvis showed no acute pathology. She was treated with increased pantoprazole and initiation of sucralfate, with symptom improvement. Her transaminitis remained at baseline and was attributed to GVHD. Chronic hip pain was managed with oxycodone. Medication reconciliation was completed with patient and family education. She stabilized and was discharged home with updated medication instructions and follow-up plans.",
    "problems": [
      "Other specified gastritis, without mention of hemorrhage",
      "Complications of transplanted bone marrow",
      "Chronic graft-versus-host disease",
      "Acute myeloid leukemia, in remission",
      "Adrenal cortical steroids causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Nonspecific elevation of levels of transaminase or lactic acid dehydrogenase [LDH]",
      "Pain in joint, pelvic region and thigh",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Personal history of tuberculosis",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism"
    ]
  }
}
